  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If the last time you played VRChat, your game was in full screen on your secondary display, the game will simply not boot anymore (press play in steam, unity crash window, then closes.) You have to completely clean the VRChat registry keys or know enough to disable fullscreen using regedit to actually boot up the game again.\nRepro Steps: using a secondary display, move the VRChat window to that second monitor, then do alt+enter to enter fullscreen. Then, close the game. Try to boot the game back.\nExpected: The game opens up successfully.\nActual: The game simply cannot boot, get a unity crash window and that's it.\nI have troubleshooted multiple situations on my main PC, it's the only one with two monitors I own (one 4K, one 1080p) and I didn't really have anyone else with a dual monitor setup to test it with.\nHere is a Twitch VOD of me troubleshooting the issue (crash at the end when executing what I said in repro steps): https://www.twitch.tv/videos/1141077748",
